mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067725/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-161359" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{u}^{2}+uv-{v}^{2}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067725/state.json" "file_sha256" "b65937d72afce5260534d53d0c48a0a2dadbce7b5a63ad0dc73a4e54242f6b9c" "basis" 2263 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067725/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-161359" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{u}^{2}-uv+{v}^{2}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067725/state.json" "file_sha256" "b65937d72afce5260534d53d0c48a0a2dadbce7b5a63ad0dc73a4e54242f6b9c" "basis" 2263 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067725/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-161359" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{u}^{2}-{v}^{2}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067725/state.json" "file_sha256" "b65937d72afce5260534d53d0c48a0a2dadbce7b5a63ad0dc73a4e54242f6b9c" "basis" 2263 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067725/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-161462" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨z,\\,y+2z,\\,2x-y⟩$ and the surface $S$ defined by $z=y-x$ for $0\\le x\\le 2$ and $-1\\le y\\le 2.$ Using the parametrization $x=u$ and $y=v,$ the flux of $F$ through $S$ can be expressed as \n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067725/state.json" "file_sha256" "b65937d72afce5260534d53d0c48a0a2dadbce7b5a63ad0dc73a4e54242f6b9c" "basis" 2263 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067725/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-161462" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nUsing the parametrization, where $x=u$ and $y=v,$ our surface can be parameterized as\n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u,\\,v,\\,v-u⟩\n$$\n\nover the domain \n\n$$\nD={(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 2,\\,-1\\le v\\le 2}.\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v-u)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,-1⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v-u)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,-1,\\,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & =⟨z,\\,y+2z,\\,2x-y⟩{|}_{x=u,\\,\\,y=v,\\,\\,z=v-u} \\\\  & =⟨v-u,\\,v+2(v-u),\\,2u-v⟩ \\\\  & =⟨v-u,\\,3v-2u,\\,2u-v⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨v-u,\\,3v-2u,\\,2u-v⟩\\cdot ⟨1,\\,-1,\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =(v-u)\\cdot 1+(3v-2u)\\cdot (-1)+(2u-v)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =v-u-3v+2u+2u-v \\\\  & =3u-3v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨z,\\,y+2z,\\,2x-y⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(3u-3v)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}(3u-3v)\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067725/state.json" "file_sha256" "b65937d72afce5260534d53d0c48a0a2dadbce7b5a63ad0dc73a4e54242f6b9c" "basis" 2263 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067725/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-161462" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067725/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "fcc6e5e5dace3db1f93bc869d01232d35269ed72008a5716d4c43f6c74c60799" "basis" 2263 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067725/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-161462" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067725/state.json" "file_sha256" "b65937d72afce5260534d53d0c48a0a2dadbce7b5a63ad0dc73a4e54242f6b9c" "basis" 2263 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067725/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-161462" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "2u+v"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067725/state.json" "file_sha256" "b65937d72afce5260534d53d0c48a0a2dadbce7b5a63ad0dc73a4e54242f6b9c" "basis" 2263 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067725/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-161462" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "2u-3v"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067725/state.json" "file_sha256" "b65937d72afce5260534d53d0c48a0a2dadbce7b5a63ad0dc73a4e54242f6b9c" "basis" 2263 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067725/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-161462" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "3u-3v"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067725/state.json" "file_sha256" "b65937d72afce5260534d53d0c48a0a2dadbce7b5a63ad0dc73a4e54242f6b9c" "basis" 2263 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067725/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-161462" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "3v+u"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067725/state.json" "file_sha256" "b65937d72afce5260534d53d0c48a0a2dadbce7b5a63ad0dc73a4e54242f6b9c" "basis" 2263 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067725/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-161462" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "u+2v"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067725/state.json" "file_sha256" "b65937d72afce5260534d53d0c48a0a2dadbce7b5a63ad0dc73a4e54242f6b9c" "basis" 2263 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067725/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-161462" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3u-3v"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067725/state.json" "file_sha256" "b65937d72afce5260534d53d0c48a0a2dadbce7b5a63ad0dc73a4e54242f6b9c" "basis" 2263 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067725/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-161357" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨x+y,\\,2x-y,\\,x+z⟩$ and the surface $S$ defined by $z=2x-2y$ for $0\\le x\\le 2$ and $-1\\le y\\le 2.$ Using the parametrization $x=u$ and $y=v,$ the flux of $F$ through $S$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067725/state.json" "file_sha256" "b65937d72afce5260534d53d0c48a0a2dadbce7b5a63ad0dc73a4e54242f6b9c" "basis" 2263 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067725/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-161357" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nUsing the parametrization, where $x=u$ and $y=v,$ our surface can be parameterized as\n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u,\\,v,\\,2u-2v⟩\n$$\n\nover the domain \n\n$$\nD={(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 2,\\,-1\\le v\\le 2}.\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(2u-2v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,2⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(2u-2v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,-2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2,\\,2,\\,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & =⟨x+y,\\,2x-y,\\,x+z⟩{|}_{x=u,\\,\\,y=v,\\,\\,z=2u-2v} \\\\  & =⟨u+v,\\,2u-v,\\,u+(2u-2v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨u+v,\\,2u-v,\\,3u-2v⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨u+v,\\,2u-v,\\,3u-2v⟩\\cdot ⟨-2,\\,2,\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =(u+v)\\cdot (-2)+(2u-v)\\cdot (2)+(3u-2v)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-2u-2v+4u-2v+3u-2v \\\\  & =5u-6v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨x+y,\\,2x-y,\\,x+z⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(5u-6v)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}(5u-6v)\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067725/state.json" "file_sha256" "b65937d72afce5260534d53d0c48a0a2dadbce7b5a63ad0dc73a4e54242f6b9c" "basis" 2263 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067725/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-161357" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067725/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "fcc6e5e5dace3db1f93bc869d01232d35269ed72008a5716d4c43f6c74c60799" "basis" 2263 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067725/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-161357" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067725/state.json" "file_sha256" "b65937d72afce5260534d53d0c48a0a2dadbce7b5a63ad0dc73a4e54242f6b9c" "basis" 2263 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067725/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-161357" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "-2u+v"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067725/state.json" "file_sha256" "b65937d72afce5260534d53d0c48a0a2d